/// Common superclass for row-source device schemas (PRD "Baustein 1").
///
/// A device schema describes ONE device type — its columns and the OPC UA node
/// names they resolve against — and carries no reference to any concrete device.
/// The same schema is reused across N identical devices; the binding to a device
/// is just an OPC UA node path, supplied at runtime via the adapter's
/// DeviceNodePaths setting and resolved by name (see OPCUA.DataSource.Resolver).
///
/// Every schema generated by the wizard or by the /schemas REST endpoint extends
/// this class. Beyond what it inherits from <class>OPCUA.DataSource.Definition</class>,
/// its purpose is to give the DataSourceClass setting a precise, filterable class
/// family for its Production Configuration dropdown: narrowing the dropdown to
/// this class excludes the hand-authored Examples and OPCUA.Tests classes, which
/// also extend Definition but would fail in a row-source service.
Class OPCUA.DataSource.DeviceSchema Extends OPCUA.DataSource.Definition [ Abstract, NoExtent ]
{

}
